A||N||10||bHooper||So whats wrong with this Auto Tranny?||||5||
Z||000000||bHooper||10-19-2001||03:15 PM||||my SE is about to drive me bonkers!  it is an '86 v-6 wiht 159,000 miles on it.  i got it from Doug Kinney in May.<P>since June I have expereinced the following problems with the tranny:<BR>1) Random whirring noise (this began after i changed the fluid and fliter in the tranny).  the noise wasnt constant, it was kind of a ghost.<BR>2)attempted to fix noise by upgrading the filter to a Carquest and replacing the fluid.  the noise didn't occure for a week until today!<BR>3) since fliter change #2, the car feels as if it is slipping in gear (from time to time).<BR>4) and today, the car will ocaisionally shudder and stall when i come to a stop, plus hang up in gear (some of the time).<P>So, whats wrong with this thing?  Torque convertor?  Selonoid?  Me?  What?<P>It wouldn't bother me so bad if the car were a complete rag, but accept for a few things, it is pretty nice.<P><BR>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||10-19-2001||03:20 PM||||oh yeah, i forgot to add.  the temp gauge seems to rise a bit when the car is stopped.  it didn't do that b4.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaveL||10-19-2001||03:25 PM||||One thing you need to do is adjust your throttle valve cable. If it isn't set up right, it can cause all sorts of odd shifting problems.  If you aren't sure how to do it, just do a search, there is a wealth of info on it. My tranny was acting as though it was about to go completely until I adjusted this<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||10-19-2001||03:31 PM||||Did you put the right type of fluid in it???  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||10-19-2001||09:14 PM||||the throttle valve cable?  whats that?  where is it?  and how do i adjust it?<P>i am using dexron III.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||10-24-2001||11:30 AM||||would the Detent / TV cable cause the car to shudder and stall?<P>if i'm going to replace this, i might as well replace the selonoid too, right?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||10-24-2001||01:37 PM||||Try pulling lightly on the casing where the cable goes into the transmission, see if it moves, it should all be firmly attached.  My cable had got disconnected from the top of the trans and caused really hard shifting and sometimes it wouldn't get out of first.  The problem could also be the cables near the throttle body getting hung up on something.  Try wiggling them around an make sure they all move smootly back and forth.<P>Because my cable was just bad, I got a replacement and had it installed for cheap and has worked great sinse then.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||10-29-2001||08:08 PM||||ok, so i got a new cable ($16.99 from Pep Boys) and intend on fixing this thing later this week.<P>is it possible for the detient cable to cause the car to shudder and stall?  i understand that it could create the other problems i am experienceing.<P>thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Juiced_V8||10-29-2001||09:01 PM||||seen it a hundred times <BR>the shudder and stall as you roll to a stop, tcc switch (torque converter solinoid) its the electronic part under the valve body cover ..also while your there i strongly suggest a trans go shift kit it isnt a shift modifier kit it corrects common problems used it on my 86 v8 worked great!!good luck to you<P>------------------<BR>86 gt v8 fogger set up sold going to get a simple sniper system with a plate||||reg||12
Z||000009||bHooper||11-02-2001||10:16 AM||||I'll be John Brown!  That darned detent cable just attach's to a little wire coming out of a hole in the transmision housing?!  No retaining clip or nothing!<P>Jebus!  <P>Also, my Motormite cable is about 2' shorter than the factory, so I am routing it differently.||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||11-02-2001||11:26 AM||||Stupid Motormite cable!  It slips out of adjustment!  i just took the car for a spin, and it hangs in gear up to 4000 rpms until i let off of the throttle!<P>i'm ordering one from the fiero store... like i should have done in the first place!<P>but, i truely believe, that that is the root of all my problems, haing gone from a worn out original to a new "cheapo" cable.  it should be fine once i figure out how to adjust the cable properly.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
